===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂weh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|winge}}, {{m|enm|wenge}}, from {{der|en|non|vængr}} {{gl|"wing of a flying animal, wing of a building"; compare {{m|non|vængi|t=ship's cabin}}}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wēingijaz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂weh₁-|t=to blow}}, thus related to {{m|en|wind}}. Cognate with {{cog|da|vinge||wing}}, {{cog|sv|vinge||wing}}, {{cog|is|vængur||wing}}.

Replaced native {{ncog|enm|fither}} (from {{ncog|ang|fiþre}}, from {{ncog|gem-pro|*fiþriją}}), which merged with {{m+|enm|fether}} (from {{m+|ang|feþer}}, from {{cog|gem-pro|*feþrō}}). More at {{m|en|feather}}.

