===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[appendage]] of an [[animal]]'s (bird, bat, insect) body that enables it to fly.
#: {{ux|en|The bird was flapping its '''wings'''}}
# A [[fin]] at the side of a [[ray]] or similar fish.
# {{senseid|en|arm}} {{lb|en|slang}} Human [[arm]].
# {{lb|en|aviation}} Part of an [[aircraft]] that produces the lift for rising into the air.
#: {{ux|en|I took my seat on the plane, overlooking the '''wing'''.}}
# One of the large [[pectoral]] [[fin]]s of a [[flying fish]].
# One of the broad, thin, [[anterior]] [[lobe]]s of the foot of a [[pteropod]], used as an [[organ]] in swimming.
# {{lb|en|botany}} Any [[membranaceous]] expansion, such as that along the sides of certain stems, or one of the [[bract]]s on a [[dragon fruit]], or of a fruit of the kind called [[samara]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} Either of the two side [[petal]]s of a [[papilionaceous]] [[flower]].
# A side shoot of a tree or plant; a branch growing up by the side of another.
# Passage by flying; flight.
#: {{ux|en|to take '''wing'''}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|III|ii|passage=Light thickens; and the crow / Makes '''wing''' to the rooky wood.}}
# Limb or instrument of flight; means of flight or of rapid motion.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3|IV|iii|passage=Fiery expedition be my '''wing'''.}}
# A part of something that is lesser in size than the main body, such as an [[extension]] from the main building.
#: {{ux|en|the west '''wing''' of the hospital}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''wings''' of a corkscrew}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Laura Bates|title=Girl Up|page=8
|passage=It's a bit annoying but (like sanitary pads with '''wings''') it's worth it if you want to stay extra secure.}}
# One of the longer sides of [[crownwork]]s or [[hornwork]]s in [[fortification]].
# {{lb|en|slang|MLE}} {{short for|en|[[prison]] [[wing]]|nodot=1}}, a [[cellblock]]; or [[prison]] or [[do time|doing time]] by extension.
#* {{quote-song|en|date=18-07-2021|lyricist=Trizz|title=‘Woop’ Freestyle|time=0:25|passage=They got bro-bro stuck on the '''wing''', cah I picked up and bullet him}}
# Anything that agitates the air as a wing does, or is put in winglike motion by the action of the air, such as a fan or vane for winnowing grain, the vane or sail of a windmill, the sail of a ship, etc.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|IX||Fair ship, that from the Italian shore,<br>⁠Sailest the placid ocean-plains<br>⁠With my lost Arthur’s loved remains,<br>Spread thy full '''wings''', and waft him o’er.}}
# A protruding piece of material on a menstrual [[pad]] to hold it in place and prevent [[leakage]].
# An ornament worn on the shoulder; a small [[epaulet]] or shoulder knot.
# A [[cosmetic]] effect where [[eyeliner]] curves outward and ends at a point.
# A faction of a [[political]] movement. Usually implies a position apart from the mainstream [[center]] position.
# An organizational grouping in a [[military]] [[aviation]] service:
## {{lb|en|British}} A unit of command consisting of two or more [[squadron]]s and itself being a sub-unit of a [[group]] or [[station]].
## {{lb|en|US}} A larger formation of two or more groups, which in turn control two or more squadrons.
# {{lb|en|British}} A panel of a car which encloses the wheel area, especially the front wheels.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[platform]] on either side of the [[bridge]] of a [[vessel]], normally found in pairs.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} That part of the [[hold]] or [[orlop]] of a vessel which is nearest the sides. In a fleet, one of the extremities when the ships are drawn up in line, or when forming the two sides of a triangle.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1864|author=William M. Brady|title=The Kedge-anchor|passage= their ends may rest a little below the orlop-'''wing''' gratings}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[position]] in several field games on either side of the field.
#: {{ux|en|Smith started the game in the centre of midfield, but moved to the '''wing''' after 30 minutes.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A player occupying such a position, also called a [[winger]]
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 2, 2011| title=Wales 2-1 Montenegro| work=BBC| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/14660870.stm| passage=The Tottenham '''wing''' was causing havoc down the right and when he broke past the bemused Sasa Balic once again, {{w|Craig Bellamy|Bellamy}} was millimetres from connecting with his cross as the Liverpool striker hurled himself at the ball.}}
# {{lb|en|typography|informal|rare}} A [[háček]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1985|author=David Grambs|title=Literary Companion Dictionary|pageurl=http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PUYOAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA378&dq=%22wing%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=fGU0T4HDB6Ot0QX7rKWaAg&ved=0CGQQ6AEwCQ#v=onepage&q=%22wing%22&f=false|page=378
|passage=ˇ '''wing''', wedge, hǎcek, inverted circumflex (''Karel Čapek'')}}
# {{senseid|en|theater}} {{lb|en|theater}} One of the [[unseen]] [[area]]s on the side of the [[stage]] in a [[theatre]].
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Redheap|page=176|passage=The performers crowded breathlessly in the '''wings'''.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} The [[insignia]] of a [[qualified]] [[pilot]] or [[aircrew]] member.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=[[w: Chris Wallace (journalist)|Chris Wallace]]|title=Character: Profiles in Presidential Courage
|passage=Anyone and everyone with '''wings''' - press officers, operations specialists, even General {{w|Curtis LeMay}}, commander of the U.S. Air Force in Europe - was put on flight duty and took turns flying double shifts for "[[w:Berlin Blockade|Operation Vittles]]."}}
# A [[portable]] [[shelter]] consisting of a [[fabric]] [[roof]] on a frame, like a [[tent]] without sides.
# On the [[enneagram]], one of the two [[adjacent]] [[type]]s to an [[enneatype]] that forms an [[individual]]'s [[subtype]] of his or her enneatype.
#: {{ux|en|Tom's a 4 on the enneagram, with a 3 '''wing'''.}}

